    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Choosing Read-Only in a settings screen feels different from seeing a modification blocked in a real tool. DBeaver continued to work for reads while changes were denied."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Remember the direct UPDATE that succeeded. If direct database access and original credentials remain available, QueryPie user privileges do not govern that route. Production adoption requires restricting permitted connection sources and managing source accounts too."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Read-only does not itself prevent data leakage. Which data is visible, how much can be read, and whether results can be copied or exported require separate checks. This article tested reads, UPDATE, and revocation only."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When evaluating adoption, test with the development team’s actual tools rather than stopping at configuration. Check that prohibited queries are blocked, observe existing connections after revocation, and find those actions again in the audit view."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "attrs": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Next: Requesting the Privileges I Need"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Here, the administrator granted and revoked privileges directly. A real company needs a workflow where users request access and a designated person approves it, rather than contacting an administrator ad hoc each time."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Next, I will follow a developer’s database access request through approval, including time-limited access and what changes in the user view after approval."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " "
        }
      ]
    }
